Z||000021||northstar87||06-27-2001||11:34 PM||||I have 2 88 GT T-TOPS and love them.  I bought one with only 19,000 miles and it was in such great shape.  Still had the original GT+4 on them. The guy who owned this car had marked down every gas fill up and service since it had 12 miles on it.   I just did not want to put the miles on this one because I think this will be one of the most desirable Fiero's out there.  I bought another in Detroit which was the same color and everything.  Red.  I now drive this car every day.  I love it to death.  The T-TOP's are great!  <P>Chris Moore||||reg||1
Z||000022||Songman||06-28-2001||12:01 AM||||Great cars! I knew there were quite a few T-tops on here...<P>Archie, I would still love to make mine into a Finale. Just no funds right now, so the Indy clone is more in the pocketbook range. Someone asked a good question elsewhere about the trunk. Can you get to it on these cars?<P>Okay, sour lemon... we're running pretty close together here. Is your dashboard at least bolted in? Mine's not.. hehe Don't know about the seats. The seatcovers hide them. I did put a console in. The back part anway where I put my arm. No shifter surround at all. No radio or radio surround. No vents. No speaker covers. No side covers (up beside each seat). And everything that is there has been spray painted black... And not very well either!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000023||Sour Lemon||06-28-2001||01:09 AM||||I still have my dash in, but...<P>Everything is mildewy,  one of the seats is missing, the center console is gone,  the headliner is in shreds, the front end was hit by a dear so the fascia needs to get replaced, the winshield is cracked, and the notchback clip is busted in 3 places.<BR>The wonders of a project car  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||10
